{
  "//": [
    "LINT-1 (CI1-L2): the ONE TypeScript program that gives eslint.config.mjs's typed block its type",
    "information (@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises). Lint only: it never emits, and it is deliberately",
    "not named tsconfig.json, so editors and the TypeScript project service never pick it up.",
    "include: exactly the typed block's `files` globs. A file that block lints but this program lacks fails",
    "lint with a parsing error; it is never silently linted without types.",
    "paths: every alias of every other tsconfig in the repository, with the same target, written relative to",
    "this file (no baseUrl). A suite's alias missing here would resolve to an error type (a suite has no",
    "node_modules link to fall back on), and the rule would then silently skip that module's promises.",
    "test/unit/tooling/lint-typed-program.test.ts fails when either list drifts."
  ],
  "extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "types": ["node"],
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": false,
    "paths": {
